#### Types of Variables :- 

##### 1.Local Variables

  - Declared inside a function or block

  - Accessible only within that block

  - Not automatically initialized (contains garbage value)
  ```c++
  void func() {
      int a;  // local variable
  }
  ```
#### 2.Global Variables
- Declared outside all functions
- Accessible from any function in the same file
- Automatically initialized to 0
``` c++ 
int g=10; 
void main(){

}
```
#### 3.Static Variables

- Value is preserved between function calls

- Default value = 0

- Can be inside a function or globally
``` c++ 
void test() {
    static int count = 0;
    count++;
}
```
#### 4. Extern Variables

- Declares a variable that is defined in another file

- No memory allocation (just a declaration)
``` c++
extern int x; // defined elsewhere
```
#### 5. Register Variables

Suggests storing the variable in CPU register for speed

Compiler may ignore it

Cannot take its address (&)

register int speed;

6️⃣ Mutable Variables (C++ only)

Used inside const classes

Allows modification even when the object is const

class Test {
public:
    mutable int x;
};

7️⃣ Reference Variables (C++ only)

Another name for an existing variable

int a = 10;
int &ref = a;

8️⃣ Constant Variables

Value cannot change after initialization

const int MAX = 100;

9️⃣ Volatile Variables

Tells the compiler that the variable can change unexpectedly
(used in hardware / multi-threading)

volatile int flag;

``` c++ 
int a;          // global → value = 0
void fun() {
    int b;      // local → garbage
    static int c; // static → 0
}
```




| Variable Type | Scope                 | Lifetime              | Example             |
| ------------- | --------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------- |
| Local         | Block                 | During block          | `int x;`            |
| Global        | Entire program        | Entire program        | `int g;`            |
| Static        | Block or global       | Entire program        | `static int count;` |
| Extern        | Depends on definition | Depends on definition | `extern int x;`     |
| Register      | Block                 | Block                 | `register int r;`   |
| Constant      | Depends               | Depends               | `const int N;`      |
| Reference     | Block                 | Block                 | `int &ref = a;`     |
| Mutable       | Class object          | Object’s life         | `mutable int x;`    |